{
  "id": "COMPOUND:40343 - PROTEIN:813",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests that Monotiporic Acid B interacts with the Kappa-type opioid receptor through a shared target of 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C. This receptor is targeted by multiple compounds, including Ginkgolide A and 3-Methylfentanyl, all of which are linked to the Kappa-type opioid receptor. Monotiporic Acid B, through its interaction with 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, appears to be part of a broader network of compounds that ultimately engage the Kappa-type opioid receptor. The consistent presence of 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C as a common target across these pathways indicates a potential mechanism involving receptor activation or modulation. The evidence supports a relationship where Monotiporic Acid B may influence the Kappa-type opioid receptor via this intermediary receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
